From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:44:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 5/6] media: qcom: camss: Add SC7180 CSIPHY D-PHY lane
 settings

The base SC7180 CAMSS support has no CSIPHY lane register table, so the
D-PHY cameras never got their PHY programmed. Add the SC7180 (CSIPHY
v1.2) 2-phase D-PHY lane register table (clock + four data lanes) and
wire CAMSS_7180 into the D-PHY branch of csiphy_lanes_enable().

The table is taken from the Qualcomm downstream CSIPHY v1.2 register set
and uses the chip's absolute register map. The C-PHY branch is added in a
follow-up patch.

---
 .../qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c         | 135 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 135 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
index 54b3d1a5e295..3320c20df766 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
@@ -293,6 +293,132 @@ csiphy_lane_regs lane_regs_sdm845_3ph[] = {
 	{CSIPHY_LN5_CSI_3PH_CTRLn_ADDR(55), 0x51, 0x00, CSIPHY_DEFAULT_PARAMS},
 };
 
